105855	105938	105573	105574	Charles Hatfield	415	“ When I beheld my mother weep -- heard her implore and beseech -- and was made aware of the ruin that threatened her unless I agreed to the proposals of this unknown suitor , I wept also -- and , my tears choking me , my silence was taken for assent . Then my mother departed to visit her solicitor : and in my despair I despatched a note to you , praying you to call on me during her absence . ”
